    summary: "Hypomethylating agents de-repress endogenous retroviruses and cancer-testis antigens and induce viral mimicry through interferon signalling, and HDAC or EZH2 inhibition can restore antigen presentation machinery. Trials combining epigenetic agents with checkpoint blockade in colorectal and lung cancer have been mostly small, with variable schedules and no pharmacodynamic gating. Dose and schedule, rather than the concept, are probably the reason for inconsistency.",
